# Build context = cms-frontend, so the repo-root .dockerignore does not apply.
#
# `node_modules` is the load-bearing line: the Dockerfile runs `npm install` and only THEN
# `COPY . .`, so without this the host's tree lands on top of the install and the image builds
# against whatever a developer has on disk. ai-gateway's image failed exactly this way on
# 2026-08-02. This app is on TypeScript 7 deliberately (the React 19 + TS 7 upgrade), so the
# host copy happens to match today — that is a coincidence, not the contract.
#
# `package-lock.json` is excluded because the Dockerfile deliberately copies only
# `package.json`; shipping a lock the build never reads would only mislead a reader.
node_modules
dist
package-lock.json
.git
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
*.md
